      "writtenOn": "2023-01-26T02:25:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: prefer to use `and_then` (example in previous CL).\n\nAlso there is a compiler warning like this:\n```\nwarning: cannot borrow `*self` as mutable because it is also borrowed as immutable\n   --\u003e system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth_gatt.rs:254:27\n    |\n253 |         match self.connections.iter().find(|conn| conn.conn_id \u003d\u003d conn_id) {\n    |               ----------------------- immutable borrow occurs here\n254 |             Some(conn) \u003d\u003e self.get_mut_by_server_id(conn.server_id),\n    |                           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^--------------^\n    |                           |                         |\n    |                           |                         immutable borrow later used here\n    |                           mutable borrow occurs here\n```\n\nOne way to fix the warning is by not borrowing `conn` since we eventually just need the server_id and we can clone server_id instead of borrowing since cloning a primitive type is cheap:\n```\n        self.connections\n            .iter()\n            .find_map(|conn| (conn.conn_id \u003d\u003d conn_id).then(|| conn.server_id.clone()))\n            .and_then(move |server_id| self.get_mut_by_server_id(server_id))\n```",
      "revId": "9c74b4463061492fca80cd6430fd909276ddb8a3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
